# External live-PID rendezvous: concrete source-only successor

Architect `/root/architect_adoption_160`. SOURCE ONLY / NOT ADMISSION. This refines the external reserve of design9705 after two independently retained self-read failures. It does not change Proposed ADR-0040, decisions, full adoption status or issue runtime authority. Existing local control-plane and newly owned inert runner scope suffices after exact independent source/artifact/birth gates; no new Owner decision is necessary.

## Grounded failure boundary

Caller07/resolver02 failed at `/proc/self/stat` with EROFS before roots/loaders/graph, actual CLOSED failure20e081. Numeric method02 JS116f then failed opening its numeric own `/proc/108/stat` at line95: exit1, stdout0, stderr828B SHA78a218237b6db425bcf398f1ac544f67939b58ffc001be2c5cf03284f738d206. Outcome613B ef0b2cd501e4aa3c652186f8d367897985213301cca7b2ccd4503716e2d427c2 is UNKNOWN_QUARANTINE; entry1079B f822396dd75105ea74f955fed0c5bb4f1323a7f5237660a1640f73ea6b519e94 agrees. Retained stop0 and final sameCID607d nonrunning/Exit137 do not establish TERM-only cleanup. Numeric02's independent failure audit/CLOSED return remains a prerequisite for later effects, not assumed complete here.

Frozen sources, records, raw streams, entry verdicts and consumed authorities remain untouched. Do not restart/reuse keeper03 ce9a, keeper04 607d, or either consumed permit/admission. QEMU temp-file/self-virtualization remains an unproven hypothesis. The observed failures justify moving actual kernel observations outside the candidate process, not accepting or ignoring them. External PID1/probe03 observations alone never prove the new Node process.

## First implementable slice and exact new scope

Prepare only disabled source and hostile inert tests now. Fixed new source directories are `populated-history-target-linux-resolution-03/` and `populated-history-target-linux-runner-caller-08/`. First script `verify_external_live_process.mjs` is builtin-only and process-only: no own `/proc` reads, package roots, createRequire/SDK/module evaluation, graph, DB/SQL, network, filesystem writes or service initialization. Caller `run_external_process_once.py`, exact-buffer entry `run_external_process_admitted.py`, pure protocol/parser tests and UNISSUED templates are distinct siblings; no edits to caller07 or numeric02. Direct caller main and initial entry main/run_admitted first-refuse.

Fresh prospective creation scope `populated-history-target-linux-runner-creation-07/`, owned atomic leaf `empty-image-pgdata`, fixed container `detran-r22-161-target-resolver-keeper05`. Reuse only source controls/proven immutable bytes, not prior runtime identity. Root-issued creator permit and external exact-buffer admission bind new source reviews/path/absence/host parent identity and actual mkdir acknowledgement; ambiguous Docker create acknowledgement remains unowned/quarantined. New creator output/entry/outer scopes must be exclusive. Image88df, UID999:999, networknone, rootRO, capDropALL/noCapAdd/nonprivileged/no-new-privileges, private/default namespaces, no devices/extra tmpfs/ports and exactly three RO binds (repo, official LinuxNode, exclusively acknowledged empty leaf at image-declared `/var/lib/postgresql`) are mandatory. Do not create a PG server, RW root/tmpfs or replace a frozen source volume.

After creation, independently capture CLOSED seven-key new keeper05 birth: actual CID/image, observed bind sources/host mapping, initial one inert sleep process/PID1 startTicks/QEMU magic executable, mounted Node89af, empty owned0700 leaf inode and full nofollow parent chain. Actual toolchain/helper executable paths and bytes must be observed in this image before method issuance. No guessed PID, inode, namespace or helper availability.

## Correlation, runtime proof and closed wire grammar

New method permit adds one Root-generated cryptographically random lowercase64 `correlationNonce` to an independently reviewed closed schema. It is immutable, source-bound to one method call and retained as custody. It is a public correlation value, not a password or ownership grant. Root issuer/Engineer holder/max1/consumed0, new actual birth/creator original+returned+correction refs, script/caller/parser/entry/tools/Node/loaders/source-design refs and method-purpose are exact. Admission SHA remains external one lowercase64 arg to a closed11 exact-buffer entry; do not bake permit/admission SHAs into source.

Launch exactly one owned `docker exec -i` without PTY, supplied process env exactly LANG=C.UTF-8/LC_ALL=C.UTF-8/TZ=UTC, official `/usr/local/bin/node`, fixed absolute script and sole correlation nonce. No `--input-type`, NODE_OPTIONS, injected loader or environment selectors. Kernel NUL argv must be exactly QEMU `/usr/bin/qemu-x86_64`, officialNode, fixedscript, nonce. Logical Node argv must be exactly officialNode, fixedscript, nonce. Own process.pid is a strict safe integer >1 and <=2147483647; an emitted PID alone is untrusted until the complete external bracket matches.

All frames are UTF-8 JSON with exactly one literal LF, no duplicate keys, no accessors/reconstruction, finite exact enums, strict number types and integer bounds. READY <=64KiB, input acknowledgements <=16KiB, RESULT <=64KiB for this diagnostic; no warnings or other stdout/stderr accepted. The fixed grammar is:

- READY closed9: `kind`, `protocolVersion`, `nonce`, `pid`, `node`, `logicalArgv`, `processEnv`, `embeddedLoaders`, `scriptSha256`. Kind `EXTERNAL_PROCESS_READY`, version integer1. `node` closed10: version/platform/arch/path/sha256/execArgv/uid/euid/gid/egid; Node24.20.0/linux/x64/official89af, empty execArgv, all IDs999. Loaders exactly the three official name/SHA pairs, source actual hash. Node emits READY only after all its ordinary builtin runtime/source/env/loaders fences pass, then remains alive waiting START with no candidate work.
- START closed6: `kind`, `nonce`, `pid`, `startTicks`, `readySha256`, `attestationSha256`. Kind `EXTERNAL_PROCESS_START`. SHA values are prefixed lowercase64 and hash exact retained raw bytes (including LF for READY). Candidate validates nonce, own PID, safe positive ticks and exact READY SHA. Caller alone establishes the actual kernel attestation; Node never presents this opaque token as its own kernel read.
- RESULT closed9: `kind`, `nonce`, `pid`, `startTicks`, `readySha256`, `startFrameSha256`, `preAttestationSha256`, `runtimeFenceSha256`, `scope`. Kind `EXTERNAL_PROCESS_RESULT`; scope `PROCESS_ONLY_NO_GRAPH_SDK_SQL`. Runtime fence hash commits the exact validated READY runtime fields; START SHA commits exact consumed input. Diagnostic performs no extra action, emits RESULT and stays alive awaiting EXIT.
- EXIT closed6: `kind`, `nonce`, `pid`, `startTicks`, `resultSha256`, `attestationSha256`. Kind `EXTERNAL_PROCESS_EXIT`, result digest commits raw RESULT including LF and attestation commits the second external proof. Candidate requires matching nonce/PID/ticks/digest, then requires stdin EOF with no buffered/trailing frame and exits0. Caller sends EXIT once and closes stdin. Wrong phase/duplicate frame/extra bytes/EOF early/signal/deadline => nonzero or UNKNOWN; never default START/EXIT.

Caller records exact original READY/RESULT/stdin START/EXIT/EOF chronology before advancement. Use one connected exec stream, bounded incremental parsing and explicit phase transitions, not output scraping, sleep-based authorization or arbitrary delimiter recovery. Caller must not send START before durable proof or accept RESULT that arrived before START. Node must reject premature EXIT or a START+EXIT chunk before RESULT. Every deadline uses one monotonic absolute budget, never reset per frame.

## External kernel proof without self access

Candidate stays alive at both rendezvous points. Capture `/proc/<READY.pid>/stat` before, full NUL cmdline, full NUL environ, literal magic-exe readlink, direct magic-exe SHA/size, and stat after using distinct fixed external helper invocations in the same owned CID/namespace. Require full nontruncated records, terminating NUL, unique env keys and exact supplied3, no unsafe/Node vars; exe link QEMU and digest9376, separate Node89af file hash. Source/Node image/loaders/birth controls remain mandatory independently.

Use fixed absolute tools whose actual image paths/hashes were observed; do not assume `/usr/bin/ps`, Python, QEMU guest path or PATH lookup exists. The practical helper candidate is an exact fixed Bash program which emits its own canonical `$BASHPID` plus LF and then `exec`s the fixed read/hash tool with fixed formed arguments. Retain that actual prefix and raw payload as bounded byte ranges, require helper PID != candidate PID, and preserve full unfiltered stdout/stderr/status/argv. This explicitly proves the command targets a different still-live process, avoiding the same-getpid path hypothesis. Helper reports are prospective until exact tools/argv/exec PID continuity and error framing are independently reviewed. No wildcard helper allowlist, arbitrary shell code, indirect `/proc/self`, alternate PID or PID1 substitution.

Parse stat with its final comm delimiter and actual field positions. Both PIDs must equal READY.pid, same stable PPID and startTicks, live state excluding Z/X/x; PID <=2147483647 and ticks <=9007199254740991 in both parsers. Dynamic CPU/state counters need not be byte-equal: retain raw complete stat evidence and compare only the declared immutable identity fields, with states individually live. Exact raw cmdline/environ, exe link/hash, CID and process namespace must agree before and after. Snapshot sorted canonical numeric /proc directory inventory with bounded size; outside inert PID1, single expected Node and source-bound currently observed helper processes, any other workload is UNKNOWN. Explicit helper tuples and birth/process inventory source rules are reviewed before acceptance; name or PID order alone cannot authorize an unexpected process.

Durably fsync pre-START raw helper receipts, exact READY and canonical attestation record. Bind attestation to CID/PID/PPID/startTicks/raw argv+env hashes/exe link+hash/current Node/script/nonce and full raw B3s; send START referencing its actual SHA only then. After RESULT, repeat the complete external bracket while candidate is still waiting and revalidate the same immutable tuple, frame correlation and current source/permit/birth/directory controls. Persist RESULT and second proof/fsync before sending EXIT. The raw proof before and after plus same live connected stream and nonce prevent acceptance of PID reuse, re-exec, candidate death, wrong stream or unrelated same-name process. Any sample loss or tuple change refuses; never reacquire a replacement PID.

## Bounds, cleanup and actual acceptance

One total900-second monotonic budget begins at the one candidate Popen, covering READY, proofs, START, RESULT, second proof, EXIT/EOF and actual wait. External helpers have at most30 seconds AND remaining overall budget; polls/read/waits are <=250ms. Candidate has one900-second self timer with no phase renewal. Stdout/stderr each bounded128KiB for this diagnostic; READY/RESULT bounds above; proc data <=1MiB/file, executable size <=33MiB before hashing, inventory <=1MiB and4096 canonical PIDs. Actual tool outputs and exact protocol sizes must fit; exceeding bounds is UNKNOWN, not truncation or relaxed thresholds.

Retain Popen actual PID, times, argv/env, partial raw stdin/stdout/stderr, helper raw receipts, command spawn/timeout/secondary cleanup errors, source/permit closing and authoritative return/original/correction/entry verdict. Signals only set a flag; stop all forward phases, close stdin, and perform only qualified cleanup on the ownership-admitted exact CID. Existing receipt-finally/250ms loops/restoration-window additive UNKNOWN/permanent poison protections remain. Stop stderr nonempty, uncertainty, final inspect mismatch or still running means UNKNOWN plus unresolved-owned-running quarantine; do not kill guessed PID, remove foreign container/leaf or claim rollback. Retain final sameCID Runningfalse/actual exit values without inferring TERM-only cause. Never restart consumed keeper05 or automatically repeat the diagnostic.

The initial source slice can be reviewed with fake streams/proc payloads only: duplicate/oversize/truncated frames, wrong nonce/PID/ticks/argv/env/hash/source/loader/phase, early EOF/RESULT, multiple candidates, reused or dead PID, helper PID equality, deadline renewal, signal at consume/start/result/EXIT/write/handler restore, unknown stderr, partial writes and double-error cleanup. Immutable old failure bytes and tests remain. Source syntax and TEST_ONLY pure tests are not a process proof.

Before any new effect require: numeric02 independent failure CLOSED/returned custody; disabled new source family F1/F3 acceptance; reviewed creation source+external admission+fresh actual birth; exact observed helper/tool identities; method-specific one-use issued permit+new active entry/current four source reports; independently reviewed exact artifact pair and outer supplied3/pinned Python-I-S/raw PID+wait block. A process-only actual0/emptyerr/full connected READY-START-RESULT-EXIT/kernel attestation plus qualified stop/independent CLOSED readback is the first acceptance target. Local authorization permits that finite gate after its controls; no global installs/shared binfmt/daemon changes or generic permission ask needed.

Only after that independent actual proof should a separate `resolve_target_linux03.READ_ONLY.mjs` source use the same mechanism for builtin-only target graph resolution. Re-review its full root/4433-edge/nearest-manifest/optional-site output bounds and evidence without SDK evaluation; do not enlarge diagnostic RESULT silently or reuse keeper05/consumed permit. A subsequent source-bound resolver needs its own fresh runner/creation/birth/admission and authority. Package init/effects/Outbox/DB/populated-history/nativeCI/provider/trust gates remain separate.

## Readiness and technical blockers

No independent blocker currently establishes this design impossible under local authority. However its runtime feasibility is UNPROVEN: external helpers must read the live candidate's actual kernel proc records without the same EROFS/virtualized-exe behavior; READY own PID must map to the externally observed PID in that exact namespace; QEMU warnings cannot violate strict empty stderr; Bash/exec helper identity and pipes/deadlines must pass actual proof. Exact helper executables/source and candidate birth are missing current admission facts. Full target graph/effects remain deliberately absent. If the external process-only gate fails, preserve UNKNOWN and stop; do not add RW tmpfs, disable proof, infer native success or automatically try another method. Dedicated native amd64 runtime may then remain a separate external capability requirement, not local observed availability.
